":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.6.beta2.official [551ce8d47]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.beta2 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7680) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13600KF (20 threads) - 47.84 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI find one of my object will not be released because of `Native Refs` (\"References not owned by the ClassDB\" showed by tooltip), is this designed or bug?\n\n<img width=\"1257\" height=\"206\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4640d572-1025-4cea-bb25-7a0cf051cd80\" />\n\n<img width=\"1275\" height=\"229\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86882392-a4f9-4741-89ee-791d1e071218\" />\n\nSo, what does \"References not owned by the ClassDB\" actually mean? Is it hold by engine's GC system or something? But I don't recall that Godot\nhas any GC system.\n\nIf I manually `unreference()` this object later at some point by:\n```\nwhile obj.get_reference_count() > 0:\n    obj.unreference()\n```\nwill critial error (eg. crash) happen (after a long time)?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114548/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114548/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}